# Sky settings

option.vanillaSun=Vanilla Sun Texture
option.vanillaSun.comment=When enabled, shows Minecraft's default sun texture. When disabled, uses the shader's procedural sun disc.
option.vanillaMoon=Vanilla Moon Texture
option.vanillaMoon.comment=When enabled, shows Minecraft's default moon texture. When disabled, uses the shader's procedural moon disc.
option.sunAngularRadius=Sun Size
option.sunAngularRadius.comment=Adjusts the apparent size of the sun disc in the sky. Larger = bigger sun and softer shadows due to larger light source.
option.moonAngularRadius=Moon Size
option.moonAngularRadius.comment=Adjusts the apparent size of the moon disc at night. Larger = bigger moon and softer moon shadows.
option.atmosphereSaturationBoost=Aumento Saturazione Atmosferica
option.atmosphereSaturationBoostIntensity=Aumento Intensità Saturazione Atmosferica
option.stars=Attivato
option.stars.comment=Stelle nel cielo notturno. Impatto performance basso
option.starsIntensity=Intensità
option.starsIntensity.comment=Brightness of the stars in the night sky. Higher values make the stars brighter and easier to pick out, lower values dim them into the background.
option.starsCoverage=Numero
option.starsCoverage.comment=How many stars are drawn in the night sky. Higher values give a denser star field, lower values leave the sky emptier. The stars still fade out in daylight and behind clouds.
option.galaxy=Galassia
option.galaxy.comment=Draws a galaxy image in the night sky. It rotates with the sun and moon and is dimmed by daylight and clouds.
option.galaxyIntensity=Intensità Galassia
option.galaxyIntensity.comment=Brightness of the galaxy image in the night sky. Higher values make the galaxy more visible, lower values fade it into the background.
option.crepuscularRays=Crepuscular Rays
option.crepuscularRays.comment=Enables god rays (light shafts) visible when the sun is near the horizon through fog and clouds. Best seen at sunrise/sunset.
option.lightningFlash=Lampi
option.lightningFlash.comment=Brightness of the flash the sky emits when lightning strikes. Higher values light up the whole scene for a moment.
option.rainbows=Rainbows
option.rainbows.comment=When enabled, a faint rainbow appears opposite the sun during and just after rain.
option.endSunEffect=Effetto Sole End
option.endSunEffect.comment=Draws the End's sun as a bright disc with a flare around it instead of the flat vanilla sun.

# Clouds
option.cloudsCumulus=Nuvole Cumulus
option.cloudsCumulus.comment=Nuvole volumetrice di bassa altitudine fatte per assomigliare ai Cumuli
option.cloudsCumulusPrimaryStepsH=Passaggi Primari - Orizzonte
option.cloudsCumulusPrimaryStepsH.comment=Number of ray-march samples used to find the cumulus clouds when looking towards the horizon. More steps resolve thin cloud detail but cost more GPU time.
option.cloudsCumulusPrimaryStepsZ=Passaggi Primari - Zenit
option.cloudsCumulusPrimaryStepsZ.comment=Number of ray-march samples used to find the cumulus clouds when looking straight up. More steps resolve thin cloud detail but cost more GPU time.
option.cloudsCumulusLightSteps=Passaggi di Luce
option.cloudsCumulusLightSteps.comment=Number of extra samples used to march towards the sun for cloud lighting. More steps give softer, more accurate light gradients inside the cloud.
option.cloudsCumulusAmbientSteps=Passaggi d'Ambiente
option.cloudsCumulusAmbientSteps.comment=Number of extra samples used to gather ambient sky light inside the clouds. More steps reduce the noise in dark cloud interiors.
option.cloudsCumulusAltitude=Altitudine
option.cloudsCumulusAltitude.comment=Height of the bottom of the cumulus layer above sea level, in blocks. Raising it lifts the whole layer.
suffix.cloudsCumulusAltitude=m
option.cloudsCumulusThickness=Spessore
option.cloudsCumulusThickness.comment=Vertical thickness of the cumulus layer in blocks. Thicker layers stack more cloud on top of each other and cast deeper shadows.
option.cloudsCumulusDensity=Densità
option.cloudsCumulusDensity.comment=How much cloud material sits inside a covered area. Higher values make the clouds look more solid, lower values make them wispier.
option.cloudsCumulusCoverage=Copertura
option.cloudsCumulusCoverage.comment=How much of the sky the cumulus layer covers. Higher values give an overcast sky, lower values leave more clear sky.
option.cloudsCumulusSize=Dimensione
option.cloudsCumulusSize.comment=Size of the individual cumulus clumps. Bigger clumps read as a coarser, more stylized cloud shape.
option.cloudsCumulusDetailStrength=Scala Dettagli
option.cloudsCumulusDetailStrength.comment=How much fine noise is carved out of the cumulus body. Higher values give puffier, more detailed edges, lower values give smooth blobs.
option.cloudsCumulusWindSpeed=Velocità Vento
option.cloudsCumulusWindSpeed.comment=How fast the cumulus clouds drift across the sky. The direction is set by the cumulus wind angle.
suffix.cloudsCumulusAltitude=m/s
option.cloudsCumulusWindAngle=Angolo Vento
option.cloudsCumulusWindAngle.comment=Direction the cumulus clouds drift in, in degrees. 0 degrees blows towards +Z, 90 degrees towards +X.
suffix.cloudsCumulusAltitude=°
option.cloudsCumulusPrecomputeLocalCoverage=Copertura Locale Precompilata

option.cloudsAltocumulus=Nuvole Altocumulus
option.cloudsAltocumulus.comment=Nuvole volumetriche di media altitudine fatte per assomigliare a nuvole altocumulus
option.cloudsAltocumulusPrimaryStepsH=Passaggi Primari - Horizon
option.cloudsAltocumulusPrimaryStepsH.comment=Number of ray-march samples used to find the altocumulus clouds towards the horizon. More steps resolve thin cloud detail but cost more GPU time.
option.cloudsAltocumulusPrimaryStepsZ=Passaggi Primari - Zenith
option.cloudsAltocumulusPrimaryStepsZ.comment=Number of ray-march samples used to find the altocumulus clouds when looking straight up. More steps resolve thin cloud detail but cost more GPU time.
option.cloudsAltocumulusLightSteps=Passaggi di Luce
option.cloudsAltocumulusLightSteps.comment=Number of extra samples used to march towards the sun for altocumulus lighting. More steps give softer light gradients inside the cloud.
option.cloudsAltocumulusAmbientSteps=Passaggi d'Ambiente
option.cloudsAltocumulusAmbientSteps.comment=Number of extra samples used to gather ambient sky light inside the altocumulus layer. More steps reduce the noise in dark cloud interiors.
option.cloudsAltocumulusAltitude=Altitudine
option.cloudsAltocumulusAltitude.comment=Height of the bottom of the altocumulus layer above sea level, in blocks. It sits above the cumulus layer.
suffix.cloudsAltocumulusAltitude=m
option.cloudsAltocumulusThickness=Spessore
option.cloudsAltocumulusThickness.comment=Vertical thickness of the altocumulus layer in blocks. Thicker layers stack more cloud on top of each other.
option.cloudsAltocumulusDensity=Densità
option.cloudsAltocumulusDensity.comment=How much cloud material sits inside a covered area of the altocumulus layer. Higher values make it more solid.
option.cloudsAltocumulusCoverage=Copertura
option.cloudsAltocumulusCoverage.comment=How much of the sky the altocumulus layer covers. Higher values give more overcast skies.
option.cloudsAltocumulusSize=Dimensione
option.cloudsAltocumulusSize.comment=Size of the individual altocumulus clumps. Bigger clumps read as a coarser, more stylized cloud shape.
option.cloudsAltocumulusDetailStrength=Scala Dettagli
option.cloudsAltocumulusDetailStrength.comment=How much fine noise is carved out of the altocumulus body. Higher values give puffier, more detailed edges.
option.cloudsAltocumulusWindSpeed=Velocità Vento
option.cloudsAltocumulusWindSpeed.comment=How fast the altocumulus clouds drift across the sky. The direction is set by the altocumulus wind angle.
suffix.cloudsAltocumulusAltitude=m/s
option.cloudsAltocumulusWindAngle=Angolo Vento
option.cloudsAltocumulusWindAngle.comment=Direction the altocumulus clouds drift in, in degrees. 0 degrees blows towards +Z, 90 degrees towards +X.
suffix.cloudsAltocumulusAltitude=°

option.cloudsCumulusCongestus=Nuvole Cumulus Congestus
option.cloudsCumulusCongestus.comment=Enormi, distanti nuvole volumetriche
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusPrimarySteps=Primary Steps
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusPrimarySteps.comment=Number of ray-march samples used to find the cumulus congestus towers. More steps resolve their shape but cost more GPU time.
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusLightSteps=Passaggi di Luce
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusLightSteps.comment=Number of extra samples used to march towards the sun for cumulus congestus lighting. More steps give softer light gradients.
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusAmbientSteps=Passaggi d'Ambiente
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusAmbientSteps.comment=Number of extra samples used to gather ambient sky light inside the cumulus congestus towers. More steps reduce the noise in their dark interiors.
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusAltitude=Altitudine
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusAltitude.comment=Height of the bottom of the towering cumulus congestus layer above sea level, in blocks. It is blended into the cumulus layer below it.
suffix.cloudsCumulusCongestusAltitude=m
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusThickness=Spessore
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusThickness.comment=Vertical thickness of the cumulus congestus layer in blocks. Taller layers form the high, stacked towers.
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusCoverage=Copertura
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusCoverage.comment=How much of the sky the cumulus congestus towers cover. Higher values give more towering formations.
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusSize=Dimensioni
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusSize.comment=Size of the individual cumulus congestus towers. Bigger towers look more massive and blocky.
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusDetailStrength=Scala Dettagli
option.cloudsCumulusCongestusDetailStrength.comment=How much fine noise is carved out of the cumulus congestus towers. Higher values give puffier, more detailed edges.
suffix.cloudsCumulusCongestusAltitude=m/s
suffix.cloudsCumulusCongestusAltitude=°

option.cloudsNoctilucent=Nuvole Nottilucenti
option.cloudsNoctilucent.comment=High-altitude clouds that catch the sunlight after sunset and glow in the night sky. They only become visible once it is dark.

option.blockyClouds=Nuvole Vanilla
option.blockyClouds.comment=Nuvole Volumetriche con stile Vanilla. attivando questa opzione disattiva tutte le altre nuvole
option.blockyCloudsLayer2=Secondo Strato
option.blockyCloudsLayer2.comment=Un secondo strato di nuvole volumetriche vanilla! Attivando questa opzione si raddoppia pure l'impatto alle performance
option.blockyCloudsThickness=Spessore
option.blockyCloudsThickness.comment=Vertical thickness of the blocky cloud layer in blocks. Thicker layers stack more blocks and cast longer shadows.
option.blockyCloudsAltitude=Altitudine
option.blockyCloudsAltitude2=Secondo Strato Altitudine
option.blockyCloudsAltitude2.comment=Modifica L'altitudine del secondo strato
option.blockyCloudsRoundness=Rotondità
option.blockyCloudsRoundness.comment=How rounded the edges of the blocky clouds are. Higher values round off the blocky silhouette.
option.blockyCloudsSharpness=Affilatezza
option.blockyCloudsSharpness.comment=How crisp the edges of the blocky clouds stay. Higher values keep the hard, Minecraft-style edges.

option.cloudsTemporalUpscaling=Upscaling Temporale
option.cloudsTemporalUpscaling.comment=How many frames the cloud buffer is averaged over. Higher values give smoother, more stable clouds but smear the motion of fast moving clouds.
option.cloudsAerialPerspectiveBoost=Aumento Prospettiva Aerea
option.cloudsAerialPerspectiveBoost.comment=Extends how far the atmosphere's aerial perspective is applied to cloud rays, so distant clouds blend into the horizon haze sooner.
option.cloudsScale=Scala Nuvole
option.cloudsScale.comment=Applica una scala a tutte le nuvole, Per rendere le nuvole da dimensioni e altitudini realistiche ad accessibili nel gameplay. Se questo valore è 1.0, le nuvole sono in altitudine realistica, con il primo strato a 800 blocchi su dal terreno. Se il valore è maggiore, allora le nuvole appariranno più piccole e più lontane. questa opzione cambia pure le ombre delle nuvole
suffix.cloudsScale=×
value.cloudsTemporalUpscaling.1=Off
value.cloudsTemporalUpscaling.2=4×
value.cloudsTemporalUpscaling.3=9×
value.cloudsTemporalUpscaling.4=16×

option.cloudsCirrus=Nuvole Cirrus/Cirrocumulus
option.cloudsCirrus.comment=Planar high-altitude cirrus and cirrocumulus clouds. They are flat layers drawn overhead rather than volumetric clouds.
option.cloudsCirrusLightSteps=Passaggi di Luce
option.cloudsCirrusLightSteps.comment=Number of extra samples used to march towards the sun for cirrus lighting. More steps give smoother light gradients in the streaks but cost more GPU time.
option.cloudsCirrusAltitude=Altitudine
option.cloudsCirrusAltitude.comment=Height of the cirrus layer above sea level, in blocks. Cirrus sits high up as thin, flat streaks.
suffix.cloudsCirrusAltitude=m
option.cloudsCirrusThickness=Spessore
option.cloudsCirrusThickness.comment=Thickness of the cirrus layer in blocks. Thicker cirrus looks denser and more opaque.
option.cloudsCirrusDensity=Densità Cirrus
option.cloudsCirrusDensity.comment=How much cirrus material is present where the layer is covered. Higher values make the streaks more solid.
option.cloudsCirrusCoverage=Copertura Cirrus
option.cloudsCirrusCoverage.comment=How much of the sky the cirrus layer covers. Higher values give a more overcast high sky.
option.cloudsCirrusSize=Dimensione Cirrus
option.cloudsCirrusSize.comment=Size of the cirrus streaks. Larger streaks read as broader bands across the sky.
option.cloudsCirrusCurlStrength=Scala Arricciamento Cirrus
option.cloudsCirrusCurlStrength.comment=How much the cirrus streaks curl and swirl. Higher values give wavier, feathered streaks.
option.cloudsCirrusWindSpeed=Velocità Vento
option.cloudsCirrusWindSpeed.comment=How fast the cirrus streaks drift across the sky. The direction is set by the cirrus wind angle.
suffix.cloudsCirrusAltitude=m/s
option.cloudsCirrusWindAngle=Angolo Vento
option.cloudsCirrusWindAngle.comment=Direction the cirrus streaks drift in, in degrees. 0 degrees blows towards +Z, 90 degrees towards +X.
suffix.cloudsCirrusAltitude=°
option.cloudsCirrocumulusDensity=Densità Cirrocumulus
option.cloudsCirrocumulusDensity.comment=How much cirrocumulus material is present where the layer is covered. These are the small rippled 'mackerel sky' clouds.
option.cloudsCirrocumulusCoverage=Copertura Cirrocumulus
option.cloudsCirrocumulusCoverage.comment=How much of the sky the cirrocumulus layer covers. Higher values give a more overcast high sky.
option.cloudsCirrocumulusSize=Dimensione Cirrocumulus
option.cloudsCirrocumulusSize.comment=Size of the individual cirrocumulus patches. Smaller patches give the classic rippled mackerel sky.
option.cloudsCirrocumulusDetailStrength=Scala Dettaglio Cirrocumulus
option.cloudsCirrocumulusDetailStrength.comment=How much fine structure is carved into the cirrocumulus patches. Higher values give more detailed ripples.
option.cloudsCirrocumulusCurlStrength=Scala Arricciamento Cirrocumulus
option.cloudsCirrocumulusCurlStrength.comment=How much the cirrocumulus patches curl and swirl. Higher values give wavier, more feathered patches.

option.cloudsNoctilucentIntensity=Intensità
option.cloudsNoctilucentIntensity.comment=How bright the noctilucent clouds are in the night sky. Higher values make them stand out more against the stars.
option.cloudsNoctilucentRarity=Rarità
option.cloudsNoctilucentRarity.comment=How often noctilucent (night-shining) clouds appear in the night sky. Higher values make them rarer.

option.auroraNormal=Aurora in qualsiasi bioma
option.auroraNormal.comment=Selects the aurora in any biome mode or method.
option.auroraSnow=Aurora in biomi nevosi
option.auroraSnow.comment=Selects the aurora in snow biome mode or method.
option.auroraBrightness=Luminosità Aurora
option.auroraBrightness.comment=How bright the aurora is in the night sky. Higher values give more vivid curtains and also light the ground more.
option.auroraFrequency=Frequenza Aurora
option.auroraFrequency.comment=How often the aurora appears in the night sky. Higher values make it appear less often.
option.auroraCloudLight=Contribuzione Luce Nuvole
option.auroraCloudLight.comment=Lets the aurora light up the clouds. When enabled the clouds are tinted by the aurora instead of staying dark.
option.auroraGroundLight=Contribuzione Luce Terreno
option.auroraGroundLight.comment=Controlla quanta luce dell'aurora contribuisce all'illuminazione del terreno. Valori più alti fanno brillare terreno, acqua e altre superfici illuminate dal cielo con i colori dell'aurora.

value.auroraNormal.auroraNever=Mai
value.auroraNormal.auroraRarely=Raramente
value.auroraNormal.auroraAlways=Sempre

value.auroraSnow.auroraNever=Mai
value.auroraSnow.auroraRarely=Raramente
value.auroraSnow.auroraAlways=Sempre

# Fog settings

option.borderFog=Nebbia ai margini
option.borderFog.comment=Nebbia spessa che copre i margini della distanza di render per nascondere i chunk sullo sfondo
option.caveFog=Nebbia Caverne
option.caveFog.comment=Fine, nebbia leggermente luminsecente applicata sottoterra. Rende le grandi caverne più suggestive e aiuta a vederne meglio le sagome
option.bloomyFog=Aura Nebbiosa
option.bloomyFog.comment=Aura luminosa intensa nella nebbia. Da l'apparenza di dispersione di luce nella nebbia da fonti luminose, e illumina l'area circostante. Quasi nessun costo di performance
option.bloomyFogIntensity=Intensità aura nebbiosa
option.bloomyFogIntensity.comment=How much the fog scatters light around bright areas, giving it a soft bloomy glow. Higher values add more haze around highlights.
option.overworldFogIntensity=Intensità Nebbia Overworld
option.overworldFogIntensity.comment=Overall strength of the overworld air fog. Higher values thicken the haze and reduce how far you can see.
value.mistMode.mistModeOff=Off
value.mistMode.mistModeBasic=Basic
value.mistMode.mistModeAdvanced=Advanced
option.mistMode=Ground Mist
option.mistMode.comment=Ground-hugging haze layer. Off = disabled. Basic = two-octave noise mist with density-varying phase and wetness coupling. Advanced = adds per-step sun self-shadowing with cloud occlusion and grazing-angle cost gating.
option.mistModeOff=Off
option.mistModeBasic=Basic
option.mistModeAdvanced=Advanced
option.mistDensity=Mist Density
option.mistDensity.comment=Overall thickness of the mist layer. Higher values produce denser, more opaque ground fog.
option.mistAltitude=Mist Ceiling
option.mistAltitude.comment=Maximum altitude (blocks) above which mist cannot exist. Lower values keep mist close to the ground.
option.mistFalloffRate=Mist Falloff Rate
option.mistFalloffRate.comment=How quickly mist thins with altitude above sea level. Higher = thinner layer, lower = mist reaches higher.
option.mistSeaLevelBias=Mist Sea Level Bias
option.mistSeaLevelBias.comment=Shifts the mist base up or down relative to the configured sea level. Positive = mist starts higher, negative = mist starts lower.
option.mistShadowSteps=Mist Shadow Steps
option.mistShadowSteps.comment=Number of ray-march steps toward the sun for mist self-shadowing (Advanced mode only). Higher = more accurate self-shadowing at higher GPU cost.
option.ozoneLayer=Strato di ozono
option.ozoneLayer.comment=Aggiunge uno strato di ozonosfera regolabile (bande di assorbimento di Chappuis, 400-650nm) al modello atmosferico. Influenza luce solare, luce lunare, illuminazione delle nuvole, cielo, nebbia, foschia e luce rimbalzata dal pianeta. Più visibile all'alba e al tramonto.
option.ozoneAmount=Quantità di ozono
option.ozoneAmount.comment=Intensità dello strato di ozono. 1.00 è una colonna naturale; valori più alti approfondiscono il blu allo zenit e arrossano la luce all'orizzonte; 0 disattiva l'assorbimento.
option.ozoneAltitude=Altitudine dello strato di ozono
option.ozoneAltitude.comment=Altitudine di picco dello strato di ozono in chilometri. Lo strato reale culmina intorno ai 20-30km; strati più alti saturano meno all'orizzonte.
option.ozoneThickness=Spessore dello strato di ozono
option.ozoneThickness.comment=Spessore dello strato in chilometri. Strati sottili concentrano l'assorbimento e amplificano i percorsi radenti; strati spessi lo distribuiscono.
option.ozoneSky=Assorbimento dell'ozono nel cielo
option.ozoneSky.comment=Applica lo strato di ozono al cielo: l'assorbimento lungo il raggio visivo e i percorsi luminosi approfondisce il blu dello zenit crepuscolare e scalda la luce all'orizzonte.
option.ozoneFog=Diffusione dell'ozono nella nebbia
option.ozoneFog.comment=Applica lo strato di ozono alla nebbia: un'approssimazione di scattering multiplo consapevole dell'ozono in cui gli ordini di scattering superiori perdono più verde/rosso.
option.ozoneMist=Tinta dell'ozono nella foschia
option.ozoneMist.comment=Applica lo strato di ozono alla foschia al suolo: all'alba e al tramonto la tinta della foschia riprende lo spettro crepuscolare filtrato dall'ozono.
option.ozonePlanetBounce=Ozono e luce rimbalzata
option.ozonePlanetBounce.comment=Applica lo strato di ozono alla luce rimbalzata dal pianeta: la luce che rimbalza dal suolo viene nuovamente filtrata dall'ozono risalendo verso il cielo.
option.renderBelowHorizon=Render Below Horizon
option.renderBelowHorizon.comment=Renders the planet ground disc for below-horizon rays instead of stretching the horizon sky downward.
option.renderBelowHorizonIntensity=Below Horizon Brightness
option.renderBelowHorizonIntensity.comment=Brightness of the planet ground rendered below the horizon.
option.vl=Illuminazione Volumetrica
option.vl.comment=Aggiunge raggi di luce e variabile nebbia volumetrica
option.airFogCloudyNoise=Foschia nuvolosa
option.airFogCloudyNoise.comment=Foschia a bassa quota, meglio visibile la mattina.\nRichiede Nebbia Volumetrica!

